$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 8-Chloro-5-(3-(trifluoromethoxy)phenyl)isoquinoline (II). To a solution
of 8-chloro-5-bromo-isoquinoline (1000 mg, 4.12 mmol) in 20 mL of DMF and
2 mL of water, under nitrogen, were added
3-(trifluoromethoxy)-phenylboronic acid (1019 mg, 4.95 mmol), potassium
carbonate (1140 mg, 8.25 mmol), and catalyst PdCl2(dppf) (91 mg, 0.124
mmol). The reaction mixture was bubbling with nitrogen at room
temperature for 20 min and then heated in oil bath at 40 °C overnight
under nitrogen. The reaction mixture was then cooled to room temperature,
diluted with 20 mL of DCM, filtered through silica gel, and concentrated
in vacuo. The residue was purified by flash chromatography (Biotage,
Horizon) using hexane/DCM/MeOH (75:24:1). Desired product II (1.31 g,
3.64 mmol, 88% yield). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CD3OD) δ 9.62 (s, 1H), 8.52 (d, J
= 6 Hz, 1H), 7.81 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.68 (m, 3H), 7.45 (m, 2H), 7.38
(s, 1H). Calculated for C16H10ClF3NO [M + H]+, 324.03; found, 323.64.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery and Pharmacology of a Novel Class of Diacylglycerol
Acyltransferase 2 Inhibitors
